    "text": "Let the locus of the centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, of the circle which touches the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> externally and also touches the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>. Then the area bounded by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;and the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;is",
